Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||03:24 PM||||the 6x9's in the headrest are stupid looking, but I have been thinking of testing the feel you would get if you put a 6x9 or a 9" woofer in the seat, either between your shoulders or down by the small of your back.<P>  i had a pair of 6x9 triaxials mounted on a piece of plywood a few years back, that fit behind the back seat of a vw bug. Between cars I had it in my family room, proped against the front bricks of a fireplace and wired to a stereo.<P>  One day, completly by chance, I leaned back against the plywood board , between the speakers while some rock music was playing, and I was totally amazed at how the base, whats the right word here... penetrated your body.<P>  you could feel the base and the kick drum hits right in your lungs and abdomin, like when you go to a concert and stand in front of a speaker stack.<P>  thing is, it wasnt on that loud. I remembered this all when i first saw the stock speakers in the fireo headrests. now I wonder what it would feel like if you put a woofer down lower - to resonate your 'body cavity'<P>   one of the things on my FieroTryList||||reg||1
